Subject: [PATCH 27/36] =?UTF-8?q?hottyterm:=20Control+c=20and=20Command+c?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20copy=20a=20surface's=20selection=20too=20(SPEC=20=C2=A711)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

copy_to_clipboard takes the text selected in a surface when the terminal
has no selection; a release on a surface copies it per copy-on-select,
into PRIMARY by default. There is one selection: a press on a surface
drops the terminal's, and one on the cells drops the surfaces'.
performable ctrl+c and super+c copy only while something is selected, so
Control+c still interrupts without a selection; the user's keybind
changes them. While something is selected, the copy keys are kept from
the surface holding the keyboard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
